Sailfish alpha4 revision 3 power-key regression diagnosis

Regression:
- The #5 kernel correctly delivered KEY_POWER.
- Stock MCE short-press action requested display OFF plus tklock.
- The HD2 msm framebuffer has no fb_blank callback; FBIOBLANK returns EINVAL.
- MCE therefore reached locked/off policy while the last frame stayed visible, making touch appear frozen.

Compatibility fix:
- actions_single_on=tklock
- display_never_blank=1
- tklock_blank_disable=1
- actions_long_on=dbus1 / power-key-menu remains unchanged.
- After installing the override and restarting MCE, reset_config returned 0 for all three values, proving that they were the active file defaults rather than one-session overrides.

The panel/backlight intentionally remains on while locked. This avoids the stale-frame/touch-disabled state until a safe framebuffer blank/suspend backend exists.
The long-press framebuffer capture showed the stock Sailfish power menu; PNG SHA-256: c8c0a71417675bc06e5dcf096cfa00553e0c5918977fbc5f15f89e3724be2914.

